 "script": "Family dinner. Grandma's house is up for grabs. Homie's got the deed!\n\nTug of war! Pull! Pull!\n\nRrrip! Good news, the county keeps a copy. Bad news, nobody left a will.\n\nHere's the thing. Only forty-six percent of American adults have a will, says Gallup.\n\nSo if you inherit the family house, do this.\n\nOne. Find out if there's a will or a trust, and who the executor is.\n\nTwo. Keep the house locked, insured, and the bills paid while it sits empty.\n\nThree. Get a value estimate, and talk to a probate attorney before you sell.\n\nIf Homie can sell it, so can you.",
